91 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(In our climatic test chamber's air circulation system, we incorporate the following components and features:)/E(In our climatic test chamber's air circulation system, we incorporate the following components and features:)/Pg 10 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

92 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(1. Fan/Blower: The chamber is equipped with a fan or blower featuring a continuous-duty rated motor. This motor efficiently circulates air within the chamber.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

93 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(2. Conditioning Space: Inside the main chamber, there's a dedicated conditioning area with baffles, housing essential components like heaters and cooling coils. These elements play a crucial role in air conditioning.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

94 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(3. Uniform Temperature: Conditioned air is introduced into the main chamber to ensure consistent temperature distribution throughout the workspace, maintaining a stable temperature environment during tests.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

95 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(4. Laminar Airflow: The chamber is designed for laminar airflow, achieved using a fan motor and impeller with an appropriate capacity. This setup guarantees even distribution of temperature and humidity within the chamber, adhering to specified limits.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

96 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(5. Motor Shaft: TC/ETC - The motor shaft used for chamber air circulation is constructed with SS 304 without any joints. The motor is positioned outside the chamber, while an extended-length SS 304 shaft drives the fans. This design ensures smooth and reliable operation while preserving the chamber's internal environment.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

97 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(ATC/AETC - "The mechanical design of the chamber's air circulation motor is constructed with a sturdy shaft connected by a flexible coupling. The inner shaft is made of SS 304 material and is connected to the blower drum, which features a double vacuum seal mechanism. The motor is positioned outside the chamber, and it drives the blower drum through the inner SS 304 shaft. This design ensures smooth and reliable operation while maintaining the integrity of the chamber's internal environment.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

98 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(6. Motor Winding: For high-temperature chambers, we utilize motor windings of H class, whereas for chambers operating below 130\260C, F class motor windings are employed.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

99 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(These features combine to create an efficient and precise air circulation system within the climatic test chamber, facilitating accurate and dependable test conditions for various experiments and applications.)/Pg 10 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

