106 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Heating System:)/Pg 11 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

107 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(The chamber is equipped with sealed Inconel tube heaters to maintain a uniform temperature. These heaters are meticulously designed to ensure even heat distribution throughout the chamber. Heat input is regulated by solid-state relays, controlled through a PID controller programmer. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

108 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(One notable advantage of inconel tube heaters is their exceptional ability to withstand high temperatures and corrosive environments. Inconel, known for its outstanding durability and heat resistance, is well-suited for prolonged use in challenging conditions. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

109 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Compared to stainless steel heaters, inconel heaters exhibit superior resistance to oxidation, corrosion, and high-temperature degradation. They are engineered to deliver reliable and efficient heat transfer without direct radiation onto the test item, ensuring a uniform heating process that doesn't adversely affect the test specimen. )/Pg 11 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

110 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(In conclusion, the use of sealed inconel tube heaters is highly recommended for maintaining precise and uniform chamber temperatures while ensuring the long-term performance and durability of the heating system.)/Pg 11 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

